spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1551","id":1331009205,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85PVZa1","user":{"login":"bsdimp","id":4139006,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzkwMDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4139006?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp","html_url":"https://github.com/bsdimp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bsdimp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-11-29T17:19:43Z","updated_at":"2022-11-29T17:19:43Z","body":"The changes from #1550 don't change my analysis, though it does add an attribution requirement. here's my comment from #1550: \r\n\r\n+1 for inclusion, since it is open source or open source adjacent. Since it doesn't apply 100% to code, but rather data, I think it's OK since the clear guidelines for what is 'open source' don't yet have a clear analog for 'open data' though many standards are competing today...  I think that the restrictions wouldn't unduly interfere with its basic use or distribution, but could affected 'derived works', which gives me some pause, but not enough to reject.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1331009205/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1340259716","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1551#issuecomment-1340259716","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1551","id":1340259716,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85P4r2E","user":{"login":"Pizza-Ria","id":46799628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Nzk5NjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46799628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria","html_url":"https://github.com/Pizza-Ria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-07T01:45:04Z","updated_at":"2022-12-07T01:45:04Z","body":"Same comment as #1550 - I don't love the restriction - \"solely for education, training, research, software and hardware development, performance benchmarking (including publication of benchmark results and permitting reproducibility of the benchmark results by third parties), or software and hardware product demonstrations\" - seems to be intentionally omitting any commercial endeavors although not quite sure what the scope of \"software and hardware development\" ... is that limited to internal use? I would be against unless this is prolifically utilized to the point that not giving it an SPDX identifier creates a hardship. @zvr indicated that all the content by ASWF is under t